{
  "_comment": [
    "Generated by `hzl install` from etc/heinzel-settings.json.in.",
    "This is defence layer 2: what the unattended agent may and may not do.",
    "deny beats allow. The runner validates this file with `jq -e .` before",
    "every run and aborts if it is malformed, because `claude --print`",
    "silently ignores an invalid settings file - which would drop every rule",
    "below without a word.",
    "",
    "Two deliberate redundancies, because a rule that is silently not in",
    "force is the worst possible outcome here:",
    "  * every Bash command is denied in both the 'cmd *' and 'cmd:*' forms,",
    "    so the list does not depend on which pattern syntax is current;",
    "  * home paths are written out in full rather than with '~', so they do",
    "    not depend on tilde expansion happening in permission rules.",
    "Verify with docs/VERIFICATION.md phase 3a rather than trusting this.",
    "",
    "The sandbox below is what actually confines the agent to the working",
    "directory. Permission rules govern Claude's own file tools; they do not",
    "govern a subprocess that opens a file itself, so a Python script could",
    "write anywhere without it. Measured: with the sandbox on but the mode set",
    "to auto, both the Write tool and a shell redirect still reached /tmp,",
    "because a command the sandbox refuses falls back to the ordinary",
    "permission flow and auto's classifier approves it. It takes the sandbox",
    "AND dontAsk together, which is why bin/hzl-run passes that mode."
  ],
  "sandbox": {
    "enabled": true
  },
  "permissions": {
    "deny": [
      "Bash(sudo)", "Bash(sudo *)", "Bash(sudo:*)",
      "Bash(su)", "Bash(su *)", "Bash(su:*)",
      "Bash(doas)", "Bash(doas *)", "Bash(doas:*)",
      "Bash(pmset *)", "Bash(pmset:*)",
      "Bash(launchctl *)", "Bash(launchctl:*)",
      "Bash(systemsetup *)", "Bash(systemsetup:*)",
      "Bash(csrutil *)", "Bash(csrutil:*)",
      "Bash(spctl *)", "Bash(spctl:*)",
      "Bash(nvram *)", "Bash(nvram:*)",
      "Bash(dscl *)", "Bash(dscl:*)",
      "Bash(defaults write *)", "Bash(defaults write:*)",
      "Bash(crontab *)", "Bash(crontab:*)",
      "Bash(shutdown *)", "Bash(shutdown:*)",
      "Bash(reboot *)", "Bash(reboot:*)",
      "Bash(halt *)", "Bash(halt:*)",
      "Bash(diskutil *)", "Bash(diskutil:*)",
      "Bash(dd *)", "Bash(dd:*)",
      "Bash(git push *)", "Bash(git push:*)",
      "Bash(gh pr create *)", "Bash(gh pr create:*)",
      "Bash(gh pr merge *)", "Bash(gh pr merge:*)",
      "Bash(glab mr merge *)", "Bash(glab mr merge:*)",
      "Bash(rm -rf /*)", "Bash(rm -rf ~*)",

      "Read(__HOME__/.claude/settings.json)",
      "Read(__HOME__/.claude/.credentials.json)",
      "Read(__HOME__/.aws/**)",
      "Read(__HOME__/.ssh/**)",
      "Read(__HOME__/.gnupg/**)",
      "Read(__HOME__/.config/gcloud/**)",
      "Read(__HOME__/.kube/**)",
      "Read(__HOME__/.docker/config.json)",
      "Read(__HOME__/.netrc)",
      "Read(__HOME__/.git-credentials)",
      "Read(__HOME__/.npmrc)",
      "Read(__HOME__/.pypirc)",
      "Read(~/.aws/**)",
      "Read(~/.ssh/**)",
      "Read(~/.gnupg/**)",
      "Read(~/.config/gcloud/**)",
      "Read(~/.kube/**)",
      "Read(~/.netrc)",
      "Read(~/.git-credentials)",
      "Read(**/.env)",
      "Read(**/.env.*)",

      "Write(__HEINZEL_HOME__/**)",
      "Edit(__HEINZEL_HOME__/**)",
      "Write(__HEINZEL_ROOT__/**)",
      "Edit(__HEINZEL_ROOT__/**)",
      "Write(__HOME__/.claude/**)",
      "Edit(__HOME__/.claude/**)",
      "Write(__HOME__/Library/LaunchAgents/**)",
      "Edit(__HOME__/Library/LaunchAgents/**)"
    ],
    "allow": [
      "Bash(ls *)", "Bash(ls:*)",
      "Bash(git status *)", "Bash(git status:*)",
      "Bash(git diff *)", "Bash(git diff:*)",
      "Bash(git log *)", "Bash(git log:*)",
      "Read(__WORKDIR__/**)",
      "Edit(__WORKDIR__/**)",
      "Write(__WORKDIR__/**)"
    ]
  }
}
